    pr_ref:  # 6810
    description: "**CLUSTER tranch03-cluster-002 (MED confidence) — members F48.A1 + F48.A3.**\n\n**Mechanic**: One editorial event — when the supply-chain implementation was refactored to (a) route tests to tier 1 (not tier 2) and (b) repurpose tier 2 from \"monorepo packages / workspace packages\" to \"direct external dependencies declared in the manifest\" — the spec §14 text was not updated to match. Two specific drifts coexist in the same spec section: spec §14 row 2 still names tier 2 as \"Internal libraries, monorepo packages\" (impl: tier 2 is direct external dependencies, all `external_symbol`-kind; the 7 actual workspace packages are tier 1). Spec §14 #3 still lists `tests/, test/, __tests__/, spec/` under tier 2 (impl: tests are tier 1 with `is_test=True`, and the supply_chain source docstring explicitly notes that routing tests through tier 2 \"drowned out the real internal-dep signal\" and was the motivation for the refactor). On the self-corpus, 100% of tier-2 nodes are `external_symbol`-kind and 26,021 nodes are tier-1 with reason \"test path matches\".\n\n**Expectation**: Spec §14 is rewritten to name the new tier 2 semantics (\"direct external dependencies declared in the manifest\"), remove the test-directory enumeration from tier 2 (since tests now route to tier 1), and add a tier-2-is-NOT-workspace-packages note.\n\n**Scope**: Two paragraphs in spec §14 that drifted at the same refactor event; the `--max-tier` CLI flag's documented behavior depends on these definitions and silently differs.\n\n**Exposure**: Any consumer running `hypergumbo --max-tier 2` after reading spec §14 and expecting \"first-party + monorepo packages\"; any consumer reading spec §14 to decide whether `--max-tier 1` includes or excludes tests.\n\n**Consequence**: The numeric tier flag no longer matches the spec's documented semantics on a major class of files (60% of files in the self-corpus are tests); workspace packages are tier 1 even though §14 names them tier 2; the consumer gets a substantively wrong answer about what each filter level includes.\n\n**Source**: CLUSTER (F48.A1 + F48.A3, MED). One spec §14 rewrite (naming the new tier 2 semantics + removing the test-directory enumeration) addresses both rows.\n\nFiled via tranch 03 dogfood (passes 41-60, substrate sha256 a32c4a31..., HEAD 9a18959071). Tranch state: `~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/dogfood_tranch_03/tranch_state.json`."  # 6810
    fields: {}  # 6810
